WEBVTT

00:14.535 --> 00:15.953
Yumeka.

00:16.537 --> 00:17.705
What?

00:17.788 --> 00:20.708
Is this for real?

00:20.791 --> 00:23.711
You got a boyfriend too?

00:28.048 --> 00:30.968
So did you give up winning nationals?

00:35.473 --> 00:36.849
I didn't give up.

00:40.061 --> 00:41.103
I see.

00:41.729 --> 00:44.106
You were always good
at going with the flow.

00:44.690 --> 00:47.735
To think, you could barely
even dribble at first.

00:47.818 --> 00:50.029
But now you're a star player.

00:50.946 --> 00:54.575
With a fulfilling personal life
on top of that.

00:54.658 --> 00:57.661
That must be nice.

00:57.745 --> 00:58.662
Hey.

00:59.246 --> 01:00.956
Couldn't you have said that more nicely?

01:01.040 --> 01:02.416
I said it normally.

01:03.000 --> 01:05.544
That's why your grades
in Modern Japanese suck.

01:05.628 --> 01:07.296
I got an A, I'll have you know.

01:08.172 --> 01:09.381
Sorry.

01:09.465 --> 01:12.301
I think the elevation's got to her head.
We'll be leaving.

01:12.384 --> 01:13.886
What am I, a monkey?

01:13.969 --> 01:14.929
A monkey's IQ…

01:15.012 --> 01:16.639
I don't need your trivia.

01:16.722 --> 01:17.807
No?

01:21.477 --> 01:22.812
<i>She glared at me.</i>

01:24.939 --> 01:25.940
Sorry.

01:26.023 --> 01:27.316
Was that…

01:28.234 --> 01:29.944
An old teammate.

01:30.611 --> 01:33.155
She was at Eimei until middle school,

01:33.239 --> 01:35.324
but then she transferred
to a different high school.

01:37.326 --> 01:38.661
I've seen her before.

01:40.246 --> 01:41.831
<i>Talking about her play alone,</i>

01:41.914 --> 01:45.125
<i>she was more eye-catching</i>
<i>than Chinatsu Senpai.</i>

01:47.044 --> 01:49.338
I heard rumors that she quit.

01:50.339 --> 01:51.799
So that's what she's like.

01:56.137 --> 01:57.721
It's getting late.

01:57.805 --> 01:59.557
We should head home.

01:59.640 --> 02:01.016
You're right.

02:11.944 --> 02:13.237
About earlier…

02:13.946 --> 02:15.990
I'm sure you can do it.

02:16.866 --> 02:18.200
You can win the nationals.

02:23.122 --> 02:24.248
Of course.

02:28.961 --> 02:30.796
How many more stops?

02:30.880 --> 02:32.506
Three, I think.

02:34.133 --> 02:36.427
<i>Our shoulders are touching!</i>

02:44.643 --> 02:45.811
- Please, sit!
- Please, sit!

02:45.895 --> 02:47.855
Thank you.

03:03.537 --> 03:07.708
BLUE BOX SEASON 2

04:30.040 --> 04:31.041
EIMEI PRIVATE HIGH SCHOOL

04:31.125 --> 04:33.544
EPISODE 27
ADMIRATION

04:33.627 --> 04:35.212
Run, run!

04:36.297 --> 04:37.965
Yuki, stay on Nagisa!

04:38.048 --> 04:40.718
Don't tell me you're planning
to play like that in the Winter Cup.

04:40.801 --> 04:42.803
Kano, keep your eyes open!

04:42.886 --> 04:43.721
Yes, sir!

04:44.346 --> 04:48.142
I heard the Winter Cup
is happening over Christmas.

04:48.225 --> 04:49.518
I know.

04:50.102 --> 04:52.271
That means we have
to have dinner with the team.

04:52.354 --> 04:53.647
That sucks.

04:53.731 --> 04:55.232
Don't be like that.

04:55.316 --> 05:00.195
Last year, we got together
with our class, but this year…

05:01.864 --> 05:03.824
This year, we're practicing.

05:03.907 --> 05:04.783
What?

05:04.867 --> 05:08.037
Why would we not practice,
just because it's Christmas Eve?

05:08.120 --> 05:10.080
It's totally not because
I'm sad to be alone,

05:10.164 --> 05:11.832
or that I hate people with girlfriends.

05:11.915 --> 05:15.878
A full day of practice
from morning to evening is my gift to you.

05:18.630 --> 05:20.674
Doesn't that make you happy, Haryu?

05:21.467 --> 05:22.426
Sure.

05:22.509 --> 05:25.471
My sister was complaining, though.

05:28.015 --> 05:29.516
I'm going to go lift some weights.

05:30.434 --> 05:31.685
I'll come with you.

05:36.273 --> 05:40.778
<i>I guess he's not spending Christmas</i>
<i>with Chinatsu Senpai.</i>

05:42.154 --> 05:44.907
<i>Bad Hina. I shouldn't be eavesdropping.</i>

05:44.990 --> 05:46.742
<i>I just happened to overhear it is all.</i>

05:46.825 --> 05:49.203
<i>Clinging onto the faintest bit of hope.</i>

05:49.870 --> 05:53.957
Hina, I guess Christmas practice
is voluntary. What are you going to do?

05:55.959 --> 05:56.794
I'll go.

05:57.294 --> 05:59.213
TRAINING ROOM

06:03.342 --> 06:04.593
Haryu Senpai.

06:04.676 --> 06:05.761
Yeah?

06:05.844 --> 06:07.721
I want to ask you something.

06:07.805 --> 06:09.139
What?

06:10.349 --> 06:11.975
- Look, don't ask if you don't--
- I…

06:12.559 --> 06:14.812
Do you know Yumeka
who used to be on the basketball team?

06:16.563 --> 06:19.441
<i>Now that's a look of disgust.</i>

06:19.942 --> 06:23.737
It's been a while since I've heard
the name of the Minister of Snark.

06:24.404 --> 06:27.574
Well, I ran into that Yumeka
the other day.

06:28.534 --> 06:29.368
Chii, too?

06:29.451 --> 06:31.245
Yes.

06:31.328 --> 06:32.538
But how did you know?

06:33.038 --> 06:33.872
Good question.

06:34.790 --> 06:36.375
I bet things were pretty tense, huh?

06:36.875 --> 06:37.709
Yes.

06:38.210 --> 06:40.671
So I was wondering why she quit.

06:41.171 --> 06:43.382
I don't actually know
the details that well, either.

06:44.174 --> 06:45.509
<i>She had a lot of pride</i>

06:45.592 --> 06:48.137
<i>and wasn't really the type</i>
<i>to ask others for advice.</i>

06:49.346 --> 06:51.807
But there's no way
she started hating basketball either.

06:53.100 --> 06:54.226
Still,

06:54.309 --> 06:57.271
Chii took it the hardest for sure.

06:58.230 --> 07:01.775
<i>They'd been playing youth basketball</i>
<i>together since the age of seven.</i>

07:02.568 --> 07:05.863
You know how Chii always comes
early in the morning to practice?

07:05.946 --> 07:06.780
Yes.

07:07.489 --> 07:08.574
<i>She used to say,</i>

07:09.074 --> 07:12.286
<i>that's the least she could do</i>
<i>to catch up to Yumeka.</i>

07:15.789 --> 07:19.501
<i>Yumeka helped drive Chinatsu Senpai.</i>

07:21.253 --> 07:22.504
<i>So why?</i>

07:23.797 --> 07:26.550
<i>I wonder how Chinatsu Senpai felt</i>

07:27.384 --> 07:29.887
<i>hearing her friend and teammate</i>
<i>who she admired</i>

07:30.387 --> 07:33.682
<i>ask her if she quit basketball.</i>

07:35.017 --> 07:37.436
INOMATA

07:38.437 --> 07:40.439
It hurts!

07:40.522 --> 07:42.441
What, do you have a cavity?

07:43.150 --> 07:46.737
It's because you've been spacing out
while brushing your teeth lately.

07:47.613 --> 07:49.114
I'm going to go to the dentist.

07:49.198 --> 07:50.532
That place closed down.

07:50.616 --> 07:51.450
What?

07:52.034 --> 07:54.328
I hear the dentist by Azumabara Station
is really good.

07:54.411 --> 07:56.455
Why don't you give them a try?

07:56.955 --> 07:58.373
Okay.

08:03.045 --> 08:04.963
KIKUCHI DENTAL CLINIC

08:05.797 --> 08:07.049
Excuse me.

08:08.175 --> 08:10.302
I made a reservation over the phone.

08:10.385 --> 08:12.012
Do you have your insurance card?

08:12.095 --> 08:13.180
Yes.

08:14.515 --> 08:15.766
Thank you.

08:17.476 --> 08:19.144
Inomata…

08:25.359 --> 08:27.236
Taiki Inomata.

08:33.242 --> 08:34.743
<i>This is awkward.</i>

08:35.410 --> 08:36.745
<i>I know, I'll turn on the TV.</i>

08:36.828 --> 08:37.746
<i>It's not over yet.</i>

08:37.829 --> 08:39.831
Please don't touch that without asking.

08:40.582 --> 08:42.501
<i>What?</i>

08:42.584 --> 08:44.628
PLEASE FEEL FREE TO WATCH

08:44.711 --> 08:46.547
<i>She definitely hates me.</i>

08:46.630 --> 08:49.591
<i>Is it because she thinks</i>
<i>I'm Chinatsu Senpai's boyfriend?</i>

08:49.675 --> 08:51.468
<i>I need to clear that up, too.</i>

08:51.552 --> 08:53.387
<i>But I'm also not obligated to tell her.</i>

08:54.263 --> 08:55.764
<i>Actually,</i>

08:56.265 --> 08:59.059
<i>if only I hadn't missed my chance</i>
<i>to ask her out that day…</i>

08:59.142 --> 09:00.394
Mr. Inomata.

09:00.477 --> 09:01.520
Come in.

09:01.603 --> 09:02.437
Okay!

09:07.484 --> 09:09.361
Your slippers are mismatched.

09:09.444 --> 09:10.279
What?

09:11.863 --> 09:12.739
I'll go change them!

09:12.823 --> 09:14.491
It's fine.

09:15.117 --> 09:16.493
Come in already.

09:19.997 --> 09:22.958
This reached the nerve for sure.

09:23.834 --> 09:27.588
<i>I definitely have grounds to complain</i>
<i>over this treatment!</i>

09:28.338 --> 09:30.215
Take care.

09:30.299 --> 09:32.092
Thank you.

09:36.346 --> 09:38.140
That'll be 1,930 yen.

09:39.141 --> 09:43.145
<i>It looks like I'll have to come</i>
<i>to this dentist a few more times.</i>

09:44.271 --> 09:47.107
<i>Does that mean</i>
<i>I'll have to see more of her?</i>

09:53.739 --> 09:55.157
BARLEY TEA

09:57.117 --> 09:59.536
You're drinking juice
right after your treatment?

10:02.497 --> 10:03.415
It's tea.

10:03.999 --> 10:06.668
Yeah, it's tea, but it has sugar in it.

10:06.752 --> 10:08.420
SWEETENED BARLEY TEA

10:08.503 --> 10:10.047
You're right!

10:11.757 --> 10:13.425
You're not a dentist for nothing.

10:14.760 --> 10:17.304
I just work part-time as a receptionist.

10:17.387 --> 10:18.513
Part-time?

10:19.014 --> 10:22.059
I want to earn my own spending money.

10:23.393 --> 10:25.312
Is that why you quit basketball?

10:30.859 --> 10:31.735
I'm sorry.

10:32.319 --> 10:33.153
I'll leave.

10:33.654 --> 10:34.696
That's not why I quit.

10:36.406 --> 10:39.076
I quit because I started to hate Chinatsu.

10:41.953 --> 10:42.788
What?

10:42.871 --> 10:44.581
Plus, I was getting bored of basketball.

10:45.082 --> 10:46.583
I figured I had a good enough run.

10:47.376 --> 10:48.335
That can't be true.

10:48.418 --> 10:49.586
What?

10:49.670 --> 10:52.714
There's no way anybody
could hate your girlfriend?

10:52.798 --> 10:54.257
No, that's not it!

10:55.258 --> 10:58.428
<i>They were so close in middle school.</i>

11:00.097 --> 11:01.431
<i>But now…</i>

11:03.100 --> 11:04.226
Hold on…

11:04.309 --> 11:06.186
You didn't tell Chinatsu Senpai that,
did you?

11:07.979 --> 11:08.939
I did.

11:20.742 --> 11:22.786
Welcome home, Taiki.

11:27.082 --> 11:28.792
It's chilly today.

11:32.629 --> 11:34.089
Are you going somewhere?

11:34.172 --> 11:35.215
Just out for a walk.

11:35.298 --> 11:36.383
In this cold?

11:36.466 --> 11:39.094
I wanted to experience the winter.

11:40.011 --> 11:41.221
Do you want to join me?

11:45.016 --> 11:46.309
Where are we heading?

11:46.393 --> 11:47.352
Nowhere.

11:49.229 --> 11:50.730
<i>Judging from before,</i>

11:51.231 --> 11:53.984
<i>it's probably better if I don't tell her</i>
<i>that I ran into Yumeka.</i>

11:56.361 --> 11:57.612
I smell curry.

11:58.196 --> 11:59.197
Curry?

11:59.281 --> 12:00.115
Do you?

12:00.699 --> 12:03.702
You know, like right before you add
the roux to the vegetables.

12:03.785 --> 12:04.619
That's specific.

12:06.079 --> 12:07.706
Now I smell shampoo.

12:09.583 --> 12:10.709
I'm home.

12:11.751 --> 12:13.462
It's all so strange.

12:13.545 --> 12:14.379
What?

12:14.963 --> 12:17.841
<i>From the observation deck,</i>

12:17.924 --> 12:20.385
<i>they were all just tiny,</i>
<i>individual lights.</i>

12:21.470 --> 12:24.890
But seeing them from down here,

12:24.973 --> 12:27.100
it's reassuring.

12:28.602 --> 12:29.644
Also,

12:30.687 --> 12:32.439
I'm sorry about the other day.

12:32.522 --> 12:36.401
I'm sure my… acquaintance
made you feel uncomfortable.

12:36.485 --> 12:38.904
No, not at all.

12:39.613 --> 12:41.406
That's good.

12:43.992 --> 12:48.580
She's someone you played basketball with
since you were young, right?

12:50.332 --> 12:52.167
Yeah, since second grade.

12:53.293 --> 12:56.254
She was always like a storm.

12:57.547 --> 13:01.176
<i>Back when I thought throwing a ball</i>
<i>was the only way to play with it,</i>

13:01.259 --> 13:03.220
<i>professional basketball blew me away.</i>

13:04.804 --> 13:07.432
Mom, I want to do this too!

13:08.934 --> 13:11.186
Make sure you say hello nice and loud.

13:13.813 --> 13:14.940
Hello…

13:15.607 --> 13:17.901
<i>- Seeing someone my own age…</i>
- Go, Yumeka!

13:17.984 --> 13:20.403
<i>…handling the ball so freely,</i>

13:20.487 --> 13:23.406
<i>running down the court,</i>
<i>and carrying it to the basket.</i>

13:25.742 --> 13:29.496
<i>Seeing her able to do all that</i>
<i>made me really admire her.</i>

13:35.001 --> 13:37.170
What's up? You the new kid?

13:41.383 --> 13:42.425
You know,

13:43.176 --> 13:45.679
you kind of look like
a pawn from a board game.

13:46.346 --> 13:48.139
Board game?

13:49.516 --> 13:52.477
Yumeka! Why can't you
greet people normally?

13:52.978 --> 13:54.938
I actually played last night.

13:58.024 --> 13:58.942
Pawn?

14:00.777 --> 14:02.445
Just like that, Chinatsu.

14:02.529 --> 14:03.697
Okay!

14:03.780 --> 14:05.615
Keep your wrist loose.

14:14.249 --> 14:15.959
Yumeka's really good, isn't she?

14:16.835 --> 14:18.461
She's got talent.

14:19.254 --> 14:21.172
She sees the court so well for her age,

14:21.256 --> 14:24.509
and her ball-handling skills
are a cut above the rest.

14:25.051 --> 14:28.471
You'll have to work hard
to catch up to her.

14:29.931 --> 14:31.016
Break time!

14:32.684 --> 14:34.811
Let's practice passing next.

14:35.979 --> 14:38.982
She said we can pass!

14:39.065 --> 14:40.233
That's nice.

14:48.074 --> 14:50.577
<i>Coach called it talent,</i>

14:51.745 --> 14:53.914
<i>but I would guess that out of everyone,</i>

14:53.997 --> 14:56.875
<i>Yumeka had probably spent</i>
<i>the most time with a ball.</i>

15:16.269 --> 15:19.439
The new kid isn't getting better at all.

15:19.522 --> 15:21.524
You mean the one from Kita Elementary?

15:21.608 --> 15:24.277
Yeah, Kano, I think?

15:24.361 --> 15:26.196
She can't even get the ball to the basket.

15:26.279 --> 15:28.782
I was able to do it from the start.

15:28.865 --> 15:30.742
Plus, her passes are always off target.

15:30.825 --> 15:32.786
I definitely wouldn't want
to pair up with her.

15:33.286 --> 15:35.246
It's hard having to go out of our way
for her!

15:36.539 --> 15:37.958
I'm going ahead!

15:38.041 --> 15:39.417
Okay.

15:40.669 --> 15:44.422
Yumeka never really joins in
on these types of conversations.

15:45.882 --> 15:48.426
I bet she doesn't see much difference

15:48.510 --> 15:49.970
between us and the new kid.

15:50.929 --> 15:52.555
<i>She's a genius after all.</i>

16:05.151 --> 16:06.236
Hello.

16:07.153 --> 16:07.988
Hey.

16:11.783 --> 16:12.784
Wait!

16:19.165 --> 16:20.166
That was terrible.

16:23.336 --> 16:24.504
Like that!

16:27.173 --> 16:29.009
How do I do that?

16:29.676 --> 16:31.803
Like, swish! Like this!

16:32.595 --> 16:33.680
Again!

16:35.306 --> 16:37.642
Why do I have to teach you?

16:37.726 --> 16:38.810
Like this?

16:40.270 --> 16:41.730
Were you even listening?

16:43.773 --> 16:44.774
Mom, Mom!

16:44.858 --> 16:48.778
Yumeka's shooting is so cool!

16:51.448 --> 16:53.283
Chinatsu, we're counting on you.

16:53.908 --> 16:56.578
It's a uniform! It's my very own uniform!

16:56.661 --> 16:57.996
Look, Yumeka!

16:58.079 --> 16:59.289
I see it.

17:08.548 --> 17:09.966
It's so annoying!

17:10.050 --> 17:13.136
Why do I have to lose my starting spot
to her?

17:13.219 --> 17:16.264
I've been playing basketball longer!

17:16.973 --> 17:19.768
She only got that uniform out of pity!

17:19.851 --> 17:21.436
Calm down, Yuna.

17:23.563 --> 17:25.899
How about instead of complaining,
you practice more?

17:26.483 --> 17:27.525
Yumeka.

17:27.609 --> 17:29.778
That's what Chinatsu did.

17:30.361 --> 17:31.821
And her hard work

17:32.530 --> 17:34.407
earned her that uniform.

17:34.991 --> 17:36.409
I was born with talent,

17:36.493 --> 17:39.412
so I don't know what it feels like
to look up to talent,

17:39.496 --> 17:44.167
but I do admire her ability to work hard.

17:49.089 --> 17:50.965
<i>She was like a storm.</i>

17:51.758 --> 17:54.177
<i>She didn't let obstacles get in her way,</i>

17:54.260 --> 17:57.138
<i>and she had a magnetic presence</i>
<i>that drew people in.</i>

17:58.223 --> 17:59.891
You got a recommendation for Eimei?

18:00.767 --> 18:01.768
You want to come too?

18:03.603 --> 18:07.524
<i>She made me feel like everything</i>
<i>would be all right if I followed her.</i>

18:08.233 --> 18:09.609
I really admired her.

18:10.819 --> 18:14.781
I worked hard practicing
because I wanted to be like her.

18:18.284 --> 18:20.370
Even now,
sometimes I catch myself thinking,

18:21.663 --> 18:24.541
<i>if only Yumeka was on this team.</i>

18:26.459 --> 18:29.796
<i>It doesn't matter if it's an individual</i>
<i>or a team sport.</i>

18:30.630 --> 18:32.173
<i>Everyone's got something.</i>

18:32.674 --> 18:34.300
<i>They're all fighting their own battles.</i>

18:37.428 --> 18:38.638
You're really quitting?

18:38.721 --> 18:39.556
Yeah.

18:40.181 --> 18:41.516
<i>What did your parents say?</i>

18:41.599 --> 18:43.059
<i>It's not their decision.</i>

18:43.143 --> 18:44.435
<i>What about her?</i>

18:44.519 --> 18:46.980
<i>You know, Kano, from Class B?</i>

18:47.063 --> 18:49.065
<i>You've been playing together</i>
<i>a long time, right?</i>

18:49.149 --> 18:50.817
Who cares?

18:50.900 --> 18:53.570
Always following me around everywhere.

18:56.865 --> 18:57.907
I hated it.

19:03.663 --> 19:04.831
Rebound!

19:04.914 --> 19:06.332
Nice play!

19:06.916 --> 19:08.710
Everyone, take a ten-minute break.

19:10.420 --> 19:12.172
<i>I have to get better.</i>

19:12.672 --> 19:13.673
<i>A lot better.</i>

19:16.259 --> 19:17.260
Too slow!

19:18.928 --> 19:20.263
Where are you hitting? Right!

19:20.805 --> 19:21.848
Left!

19:21.931 --> 19:23.683
Nice effort!

19:40.491 --> 19:42.744
Why would you try to make me eat it?!

19:51.085 --> 19:54.088
I got first place in gym class today!

19:56.591 --> 19:57.508
<i>You know,</i>

19:58.134 --> 20:00.970
<i>I just can't imagine</i>

20:01.054 --> 20:02.680
<i>Yumeka coming to hate Chinatsu Senpai.</i>

20:03.848 --> 20:05.183
<i>Maybe she got injured</i>

20:05.266 --> 20:07.644
<i>and couldn't play basketball anymore.</i>

20:08.269 --> 20:11.231
<i>So she acted that way</i>
<i>towards Chinatsu Senpai to hide it.</i>

20:15.526 --> 20:16.361
Dang it!

20:16.444 --> 20:17.362
Nice try.

20:18.154 --> 20:20.114
She can play basketball just fine!

20:22.242 --> 20:23.451
That's it for today.

20:23.534 --> 20:24.369
What?

20:24.953 --> 20:26.913
Let's play again sometime!

20:28.498 --> 20:30.124
So, you still play once in a while?

20:30.208 --> 20:31.376
Just for fun.

20:34.462 --> 20:37.382
Seems like a waste to just play for fun.

20:37.966 --> 20:41.427
Everyone said you were a genius.

20:42.971 --> 20:45.306
So is that how people see me?

20:45.807 --> 20:48.685
I mean, it's true that I pick things up
faster than most.

20:48.768 --> 20:49.811
<i>Is she being snarky?</i>

20:49.894 --> 20:52.230
And I could control the ball
like it was part of me.

20:52.313 --> 20:53.398
<i>She definitely is!</i>

20:54.023 --> 20:54.899
But…

20:55.942 --> 20:59.988
<i>there are tons of people in the world</i>
<i>who are way better than me.</i>

21:01.781 --> 21:03.908
That might be true, but…

21:04.617 --> 21:06.411
Have you never thought about it?

21:06.494 --> 21:09.664
What you're going to do with your life
if you just keep focusing on sports?

21:10.248 --> 21:14.669
<i>What's the point of continuing</i>
<i>such grueling practice every day?</i>

21:14.752 --> 21:17.005
<i>It's not like you're making the pros.</i>

21:17.088 --> 21:20.049
<i>Only the winners get to go home smiling.</i>

21:20.133 --> 21:21.551
<i>So what's the point</i>

21:22.969 --> 21:24.804
<i>putting in all your effort there?</i>

21:25.763 --> 21:27.682
What kind of excuse
are you trying to make?

21:27.765 --> 21:28.891
What?

21:28.975 --> 21:32.312
I mean, all of that is obvious
from the start.

21:32.895 --> 21:34.897
Still, you keep chasing each win.

21:35.732 --> 21:38.818
We keep on chasing each shot
because it's fun.

21:39.527 --> 21:40.820
<i>I see it now.</i>

21:40.903 --> 21:43.573
<i>The answer was so simple.</i>

21:43.656 --> 21:45.158
Who cares about other people,

21:45.241 --> 21:47.160
or if you didn't play well?

21:47.744 --> 21:50.204
That's all the more reason
that you shouldn't have quit.

21:50.288 --> 21:53.833
<i>All that talent made her afraid to fail,</i>
<i>so she ran away.</i>

21:54.667 --> 21:56.044
<i>What a waste.</i>

21:56.127 --> 21:57.337
<i>It's such a waste.</i>

21:57.962 --> 22:00.340
You could've made up for it
in high school.

22:00.965 --> 22:03.718
It's natural to have people
better than you.

22:03.801 --> 22:05.345
But that's not it.

22:05.928 --> 22:07.221
That's not the point.

22:10.058 --> 22:11.100
<i>What!</i>

22:11.726 --> 22:12.727
Of course…

22:13.686 --> 22:17.231
It's easy to say the right thing
when you're not the one going through it.

23:48.948 --> 23:53.953
Subtitle translation by: Zensho Yamamoto
